11
00:53:46,666 --> 00:53:52,666
Crystal skulls are human skull hardstone carvings made of clear, milky white or other types of quartz (also called "rock crystal"), claimed to be pre-Columbian
Mesoamerican artifacts by their alleged finders; however, these claims have been refuted for all of the specimens made available for scientific studies.

12
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
The results of these studies demonstrated that those examined were manufactured in the mid-19th century or
later, almost certainly in Europe, during a time when interest in ancient culture abounded.

13
01:03:33,333 --> 01:03:39,333
The skulls appear to have been crafted in Germany, quite likely at workshops in the town of Idar-Oberstein, which
was renowned for crafting objects made from imported Brazilian quartz in the late 19th century.

14
01:08:26,666 --> 01:08:32,666
Despite some claims presented in an assortment of popularizing literature, legends of crystal skulls with mystical
powers do not figure in genuine Mesoamerican or other Native American mythologies and spiritual accounts.

15
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
The skulls are often claimed to exhibit paranormal phenomena by some members of the
New Age movement, and have often been portrayed as such in fiction.

16
01:18:13,333 --> 01:18:19,333
Crystal skulls have been a popular subject appearing in numerous science
fiction television series, novels, films, and video games.

17
01:23:06,666 --> 01:23:12,666
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
